#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e06061b-ccdb-5199-bbf5-9e833ef7c247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345696} {:answer/id #uuid "11930f00-5e4d-5b5b-b21c-251f48cea6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345697} {:answer/id #uuid "93d6df55-03b0-513a-ad51-c02435df9eca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345698} {:answer/id #uuid "a6caa2b7-ff97-55b3-8903-58b464f3a03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345699} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b19f5c-26c1-57ce-88f0-0946f12bbc8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3b19f5c-26c1-57ce-88f0-0946f12bbc8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345700} :answer-field/id #uuid "02d6925b-83d0-5682-b2df-8f48730e6d89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "272ae49c-9056-5da6-9688-ea58ac11f9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-105308" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-16{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d7e3bdc-56ae-540b-a563-de3215d488a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345703} {:answer/id #uuid "c9caf19d-a350-5b0d-9e8e-56839cea5796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345704} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3cca93-c5d8-5c9e-9326-7e616e05db3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345705} {:answer/id #uuid "ac295ca1-d020-59f9-8386-2a002c911123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345706} {:answer/id #uuid "39796869-8039-52c8-8977-eef62417ba04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39796869-8039-52c8-8977-eef62417ba04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345707} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac2ed5a-52d4-5966-b66d-bf746a1a0dfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62abef76-8742-588b-baa5-5503f357b61a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105310" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 15 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc75fe54-debb-5bdf-a270-c74fd0c6edb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117004} {:answer/id #uuid "d6737850-aa50-5861-9fd0-539c08b98ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117005} {:answer/id #uuid "db98c296-4b70-5c68-a6e0-34ad93c89ec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117006} {:answer/id #uuid "33d7aef4-cc42-58ab-93af-a2325c3d8ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117007} {:answer/id #uuid "579b15fb-4a6f-5366-8b4e-478288b504e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33d7aef4-cc42-58ab-93af-a2325c3d8ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117007} :answer-field/id #uuid "095e40bc-47ad-5518-8a85-b084b4a61a9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62e09db0-cf5e-5972-a5d2-6baa771c45b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-155967" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeb86d92-6893-5241-a76b-1b1701c15055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345710} {:answer/id #uuid "2b93dc32-8d4f-5f56-822e-a9f960e256cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345711} {:answer/id #uuid "eb582faf-85e7-5895-87c3-762111c9d3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345712} {:answer/id #uuid "f5acb448-247d-5657-860d-e3eefdfdf47e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345713} {:answer/id #uuid "aa87231d-328d-54a4-a054-83ba785a37d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb582faf-85e7-5895-87c3-762111c9d3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345712} :answer-field/id #uuid "411021a7-c86a-5aa2-a647-2fa8f052a582" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9570d4ac-8f19-5ac8-be57-aa3fad748e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-157236" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-3+4 \\\\ 5-6+1 \\\\ 2-12+10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e07eac5-1bd9-5bf4-bc54-9e7fd74e1728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345717} {:answer/id #uuid "f54e4505-f1b9-51e1-87a8-fcb6291e7913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345718} {:answer/id #uuid "0201097c-3d09-58da-9185-5d0dc7e51f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345719} {:answer/id #uuid "0108abc9-33a7-5e49-aaf5-d15d78eef2fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345720} {:answer/id #uuid "3c98a5d5-b60c-5209-9739-951c18093c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0201097c-3d09-58da-9185-5d0dc7e51f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345719} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e280f92-d26d-53f2-9892-aa9d460074f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "200acb00-0dbd-5a6f-818e-38dd5df74fbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-157256" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =4[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
